# closure_capture_scope — closure variable capture by scope
# (README §9). Tests capturing variables from outer scope.

ClosureCaptureScope is project
ClosureCaptureScope module examplesClosureCaptureScope
ClosureCaptureScope target console
ClosureCaptureScope entry main

examplesClosureCaptureScope is module
examplesClosureCaptureScope path examples.closureCaptureScope
examplesClosureCaptureScope exports main
examplesClosureCaptureScope purpose "Demonstrate closure variable capture"
examplesClosureCaptureScope invariant "Inner operations capture outer variables"

ExitCode is alias
ExitCode for Int32

stdoutWriter is capability
stdoutWriter grants write console.stdout

main is operation
main out ExitCode
main effect write console.stdout
main uses stdoutWriter
main memory heap no
main async no
main purpose "Use closure with captured variables"
main invariant "Scope capture works"

main let captured immutable Int64 10
main let okCode immutable ExitCode 0

main do printCaptured
main return okCode

printCaptured is call
printCaptured in main
printCaptured invokes console.writeIntegerLine
printCaptured arg value Int64 captured
